<title>JAPAN: Korea Container launches 2.2% five-yr samurais. [CORRECTED 10:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>Korea Container launches 2.2% five-yr samurais. [CORRECTED 10:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects name of issuer from &quot;Korea Container Co.&quot; to &quot;Korea Container Terminal Authority&quot;.)</p>
<p>South Korea's state-owned Korea Container Terminal Authority on Monday launched five billion yen worth of 2.2 percent samurai bonds due October 18, 2001, lead-manager Kokusai Securities said.  </p>
<p>The breakdown of the terms is as follows:</p>
<p> AMT 5 bln yen COUPON 2.2%	 MATURITY Oct 18, 2001</p>
<p>TYPE samurai  ISS PRICE 100 yen PAY DATE Oct 18, 1996</p>
<p>SUB PERIOD Oct 16 to Oct 17</p>
<p>SIGN DATE Oct 14 (scheduled)</p>
<p>INTEREST PAYMENT April 18 and Oct 18</p>
<p>LAST RATING AA+(JBRI)</p>
<p>LEAD MANAGER Kokusai Securities</p>
<p>LEAD TRUSTEE Sakura Bank</p>
</text>
